In a previous article, Kevin Vig <stinger@vt.edu> said:
>I cant seem to get linux to boot on my multia. It gets to the turning on
>virtual addressing and jumping into linux kernel part and then stays
>there. the harddrive goes like its loading stuff so i assume its booting

I had that problem too, when I went to a 2.2.x kernel, until I contacted
various people and asked them to send me their .config files.  Turns out I was
missing the "Frame Buffer" stuff, so there was no TGA support compiled in, so
I couldn't see what was going on at that point.

Just ask, and I'll email my .config, but the important part is:

#
# Console drivers
#
CONFIG_VGA_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_FB=y
CONFIG_PCI_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_DUMMY_CONSOLE=y
# CONFIG_FB_PM2 is not set
CONFIG_FB_TGA=y
# CONFIG_FB_MATROX is not set
# CONFIG_FB_ATY is not set
# CONFIG_FB_VIRTUAL is not set
# CONFIG_FBCON_ADVANCED is not set
CONFIG_FBCON_CFB8=y
CONFIG_FBCON_CFB32=y
# CONFIG_FBCON_FONTWIDTH8_ONLY is not set
# CONFIG_FBCON_FONTS is not set
CONFIG_FONT_8x8=y
CONFIG_FONT_8x16=y

-- 
Paul Tomblin, not speaking for anybody.
