The DECpc AXP/150 (Jensen) was the first Alpha, an EISA-bus tower, and a
pretty good machine for its time.  The AlphaStation 200 4/233 (Mustang II)
is a desktop, next generation PCI-bus system.  The Jensen is a 150 MHz
system, the Mustang II is a 233 MHz system, and should quite handily
outperform the Jensen.  Both can use ISA option cards; Jensen can also use
EISA cards, but not the PCI options Mustang II accepts.  If you can afford
to choose the Mustang II, do so, by all means, for production work.  On the
other hand, Jensens ought to be dirt cheap, if you are simply looking for an
Alpha to experiment with.

Cheers,
jwl

