I assume that you're talking about a application proxy firewall, and not
a generic web proxy ala squid. If that is what you're talking about then
you're right I don't know of any commercial firewall software for
Alpha/Linux. But there's always the TIS FWTK (firewall toolkit) of which
you need to hack a bit to get it working. Of course as you've pointed
out there's always socks....
YMMV, as I don't have any experience in both of them.

What I've experience is the Linux IPchains packetfilter firewall. It
works fine with Alpha. And no you do not need to setup gated if you just
have a single link to the net.

I think with IPchains and with Squid (distributed caching web/ftp
proxy), you would have everything you need to have a good intra/internet
setup.



