First of all, check out the pages for AlphaLinux.org, Alpha Processors Inc.
and other hardware suppliers who sell the components seperately. Installing
Linux on Alpha can be easy if you look at http://www.alphalinux.org,
especially since they address the 164SX systems:
http://www.alphalinux.org/docs/deskstation-rebel.html

I cannot address the issue of PC164 vs 164SX.

Alpha Linux distributions are curently available from Red Hat (5.1, 5.2);
SuSE (6.1 Beta) which may not be available here in the US; Debian (2.1 and
unstable 2.2). Slackware and Caldera have not released an Alpha port. If
there are others released, I am unaware of them.

Harry Heinisch



