I am posting this information to see if anyone experienced similar;
probably should alert MILO authors.

Symptom: MILO sees blank in a file system with block size 4096.

I noticed this when I rebuilt my root file system with mke2fs -b4096. 
MILO seemed to recognize the file system, but displayed total blank.  So
I copied my kernel to a floppy and booted successfully to the new root
file system.  I had to mke2fs -b1024 and all are happy now.

I doubt this is a "feature." And nowhere in MILO documentation mentions
this.  I am using Red Hat 5.2 on AlphaServer 400 4/233 (Avanti); the
milo image was taken from the CD (avanti.img).  It now happily runs RAID
on a modified StorageWorks array (the Mylex card is discarded:-).

