News to me.  I am running an S3VirgeDX 4MB PCI video card in my UDB and I
also have a 3.7GB Hitachi 2.5" IDE drive which replaced the original 500MB
SCSI.  It all works fine.  The IDE interface is giving the same performance
as my P75 laptop manages.  Its a bit slow but I have 96MB which means I
can support a fair amount of cached disc and this compensates greatly for the
IDE drive.  It is possible to stick a 3.5" SCSI drive in but then you do
lose the option of using the PCI slot and as far as I know it is nigh on
impossible to get 2.5" SCSI drives of any size let alone ones that are
several gigs in size.  Another problem with the UDB is heat, stick a modern
fast SCSI drive in there and its going to cook.  At least a laptop IDE
drive is designed to run cool.

