To be honest I haven't tried this in an alpha yet but I have multiple
ethernet cards in intel boxes at work (3 to 5 cards) and this seems
like a similiar problem that I had.

The file

file://usr/doc/HOWTO/Ethernet-HOWTO

describes in some detail how to setup two cards. The big gotchas are:
-) Order depends upon the bus numbering/probeing sequence.
-) If you have moved network cards around in a PCI bus system the
   automatic interupt assignements are more than likely messed up.
-) You need some way to make sure the cards have different IRQs.
   Or at least the first card detected has a different IRQ.
-) Mixing >A< (I mean only one) ISA and (multiple) PCI cards is a good way
   to have the first card have unique interupt.
-) If your PCI bus will be reconfigured a lot or you are supporting multiple
   configurations may I suggest a few scripts to detect which card
   got which eth number.
   2. Reconfigure the network files in
      file://etc/sysconfig/network-scripts
   3. Then initialize the network with ifup.

***) A really good idea is to upgrade to 2.2.3. I have 2.2.3 and redhat 5.2
(no  redhat patches) crusing right along. The better PCI support and  other
items are really nice.)

***) If I fremember correctly the Alpha BIOS always gives each PCI card a
unique	IRQ.(My machine is at hoem and I am at work :(	)

