In article <36E90776.3477E91@ims.uni-hannover.de>,
	Andreas Lemke <lemke@ims.uni-hannover.de> writes:

> Is there a way I can use Maple V R5 on my Alpha Linux without using em86?
> I have binaries for Dec's Alpha Unix. Trying to execute those I get a funny
> error message saying "No such file or directory" instead of "wrong
> architecture" or something like that.

Static linked binaries can be executed under Linux. So if Maple is statically
linked it works under Linux. The filessystem structure is a little different
in Linux and Digital Unix. You can change this by either adding links in the
filesystem or by patching the object file.

Andi
