Just thought to share this with you.

Multia really doesn't seem to like display adapters. I never got as far as
linux with a Matrox Millennium. I did get to X with a Trio64V+ card but it
jammed every 10 minutes or so forcing a reboot so it wasn't very useful.

I got a word from a few Multia owners that a ViRGE/DX card works for them,
so I obtained one. It works better than the Trio64 card, but recently it
has started jamming as well. It used to jam ca twice in three days when I
was running in 800x600. Yesterday I got a new monitor and jumped up to
1280x1024 and it jammed 6 times yesterday alone. The jamming is total, I
compiled Magic SysRq support in the kernel and can do nothing even with it 
after the jam has happened. It happens with both S3V and SVGA servers.
With larger screen sizes I have also noticed pixel corruption.

Today I have been trying an ET6000. ARC and MILO give messed up output
with it but work, linux console seems to like it better. As of yet I have
been unable to configure XFree86 to detect it so I can't say how well it
works. I have given up with it for now, if someone knows how to configure
it please do tell.

I've been trying some stuff that might or might not be related. I
downclocked the processor from 233MHz to 200MHz, it didn't help. Is there
some way to downclock the PCI bus?

As of late, I have been taking power for a 3'5" SCSI drive from the
connector in the PCI thing inside the machine. This doesn't look like a
power problem, but I switched to an external power source now. This far
(~10 minutes) this has performed ok. I don't expect this to solve my
problem, but if it does I'll let you know.

Riku Anttila
