Bill Johnson wrote:

> I am very new to alpha, and I currently have Linux installed but I need to
> install NT.  I don't know how to access the CD-ROM drive in order to run the
> setup program.

Bill,

You'll need to be running the ARC Firmware for Windows NT.  If you don't have
the Firmware disk from Digital (now part of Compaq) you should order it.  It,
and the FX32! program (which allows you to run Intel compiled 32 bit Windows
applications on your Alpha hardware) should run you about $30US including
shipping and handling.

Once your firmware is updated you will see an actual boot menu in the place of
the old SRM >>> prompt.  One of the choices available is to install Windows NT
from CD-ROM.

Once you've completed your NT installation, Be sure to set up the boot selection
for Linux and set it as your default boot option.  (Instructions available at
http://users.codenet.net/rjaninda/alpha.html)

Have fun!
Keith
