Depending on the alpha, Alphabios or ARC may also be in firmware. At the SRM
prompt, type
"set os_type NT"
then power cycle the machine. If the Alphabios/arc console is present it
will become the default console. You will then look for the menu entry which
stated
"Load Windows NT from CD" that's it..

But a few pointers..
1. place 2 partitions on the disk
c: size of the disk - 6mb
d: 6mb
(Alphabios) has a harddisk setup menu selection for this

2. Setup the bootpath
boot partition (system)
partition 2   path  /os/winnt40/
partition 1  path  /winnt

in AlphaBios there's a SETUP FOR THIS ALSO. you will get an error message
that there is no OS, because you have not installed it yet.

Now Install NT from CD and it will place the files in the correct
partitions. Otherwise everything will show up in the c: partition and you
will not be able to use NTFS.  The 2nd (d) partition is the boot partition.

JJ
