I have a 2.5 inch HITACHI 3.7 gig IDE drive, it is slower than SCSI but
only about 20%.  Of course, if you try and do a lot of disc access or
start trashing swap then things bog down quickly.  The solution is to
have lots of RAM (I have 96MB) which gives you a lot of disc cache to
speed things up.  The price and capacity of an IDE disc more than makes
up for the expense of extra RAM.
