KenDawg wrote in message <7chupj$5f6$1@ash.prod.itd.earthlink.net>...
>I just installed redhat 5.2 on my 4/200 233 and I wonder how can i copy
milo
>and linload.exe to the dos partition that i had to make for these?  I tried
>mounting the partitions but it says MS-DOS not supported by kernel.  Can
>someone help me in what i should do please thank you.
>

From the RedHat install guide:

Boot the system with the floppy, then run with boot disk in drive:

dd if=/dev/fd0 of=/dev/sda1 bs=10240 and press enter.

This places the milo and linload files on the dos partition that was created
earlier. You must make sure that you have set the target partitions
correctly: if your DOS partition is sda6, make sure that you target sda6 and
not sda1.You should see the floppy read for a while then it will read:
144+0 records in
144+0 records out

Reboot and set the ARC boot menu to point to the right partition.

Good luck.
Duncan






