OK so this is a hack, but it worked for me :-).

I had the same problem with an AS400 4/233 booting into DEC Unix, and had no
idea of how to get the console. One method was simply to type halt at a DEC
Unix prompt, which may not work in the VMS variant. The other method which I
found quicker was just to unplug the internal scsi HD power cable, and then
once the SRM cosole booted I just hot plugged the power cable back in. This
caused a boot error in and dropped me into the SRM console, from where I was
able to change the startup consle to ARC. You might like to installing the
DEC flash update while you are there (if there is one for your machine).

I make no statements regarding the safety of this to your system, but it
worked for me. I anyone has any better ideas, feel free to speak up.

Regards,

Matt





