Hi Folks,

I was just browsing though this newsgroup and thought I'll writ e little
repy. I have compiled 2 raytracers with different opions, inluding
different math and fastmath libraries.

There is DEFINITELY a difference in speed between the -lffm -lfm -lm
version and the -lcpml -lm version of linking (to the advantage of
libcpml). I could not get the programs linked only using -lcpml because
there seems to be a unresolved  link to atan2, which is probably a bug
in the cpml library.

However, I still have one hopefully not to stupid question:

do I still need the -mieee compiler switch ? PovRAY works just fine
without it, allthoug this just works with libcpml, RADIANCE on the other
hand needed -mieee in every combination I tried out and that was quite a
lot (se http://radsite.lbl.gov for more info about RADIANCE).

Once I have a little more time I will post some timing results.

Regards, P. Doering
