Subject: WARNING: es1370 Sound Cards
Date: 1999/03/18
Message-ID: <tcuqc7.o92.ln@snowwhite>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 456123382
Organization: Defence Evaluation & Research Agency
User-Agent: tin/pre-1.4-980618 (UNIX) (Linux/2.0.36 (i686))
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha
Summary: ES1370 based sound cards do not work on many Alphas

Hello,

Just a quick note prevent folk from wasting money as I did.

Sound cards based on the es1370 chip (basically the SoundBlaster PCI 64) will
not work on Alphas containing the Pyxis host bridge (Miata, LX164, SX164,
Ruffian).  According to Thomas Sailer (sailer@ife.ee.ethz.ch) who wrote the
driver in the 2.2.x kernels the problem is believed to be:

the es1370 doesn't support PCI target bursts, and that it terminates
attempted bursts wrongly, which causes the Alpha MB to lock up.

I tried the ALSA driver (alsa.jcu.cz) and it exhibited exactly the same
problem.  I have not tried the commercial OSS driver since I couldn't get it
to work with my kernel version 2.2.3-ac1.

Basically the bug causes the entire machine to hang whenever anything is
sent to /dev/dsp.  The mixer works fine, and I have no way of testing the
MIDI interface.

The problem is likely to also effect the es1371 which is used on the
SoundBlaster PCI 128.

I now need to buy another sound card.  Can anyone recommend a good quality
card which works with the Alpha.  I need it for recording and playing back
sound effects in a theatre, so sound quality (especially a lack of clicks
buzzes and pops as the mouse moves around) is far more important than
schnazzy wave tables.

Now, all I need to do is find someone who wants to buy a slightly used sound
card :-).

-- 
