Darius wrote in message ...
>  I have recently moved up to the 2.2.3 kernel which is guite an
improvement
>on my alphastation 200.  Anywho,  has anyone had any success with the built
>in soundboard that is "Microsoft Sound System Compatible"?  Any suggestions
>on what set of drivers to use?  Any help would be appreciated.

This is what I did to compile in sound:

yes to sound card support
no to all cards upto OSS sound modules
yes to OSS sound modules
yes to Persistent DMA buffers
no to ProAudioSpectrum 16
no to 100% Sound Blaster compatibles
no to Generic OPL2/OPL3 FM synthesizer
no to Gravis Ultasound support
no to MPU-401
no to PSS
yes to Micosoft Sound System (MSS) support
no to enable support for SoundPro
MSS base = 530
MSS IRQ = 9
MSS DMA = 3
MSS second DMA = -1
no to the rest of the sound cards

Also I didn't change MILO at all to get 2.2.3 to boot.  Though I might just
upgrade to RedHat 5.9 to get a "clean" 2.2.3 system.

- mark





