Hi Rick,

you need standard 32*8K or 128*8k SRAM (11 devices), 15 or 20ns fast.
The 32k*8 chips (28 pins) fits the smal socket the 128*8K chips (32
pins) fits the bigger ones.
PartNo. for example (winbond: W24M257AK-15, Mosel: MS62256H-15NC) for
32*8K SRAMs which you can easily find on older 486-Boards. There are
many other manufactures of these chips, but I have only these two
different ones. I use the Winbond chipy in my NoName.
I know some German dealers who sell these bigger (128*8K) chips under
the part number 611000-20 for under 6,- German Marks a piece (under
3$). I thinks these are 20ns chips. 
Till then,

Michael



