you need to use setserial and then use 38400 as the speed. It works 
fine for me...

put these lines somewhere in your /etc/rc.d/rc.local file
setserial /dev/ttyS0 spd_vhi
setserial /dev/ttyS1 spd_vhi

Then just set your terminal speed to 38400 and it will use 115kb
if you use spd_hi it will use 56kb instead. If you use lower speed
settings it seems they will do what they are supposed to, spd_?hi
will only change the setting for 38400

I ran into weird effects trying to set the speed above 38400 using stty.
just make believe you are using the 38400 everywhere and it will work
faster with the setserial line controlling the tty speed.

