Rick Brice <rbrice@xspam.gelac.mar.lmco.com> wrote:
: IMHO, it would be handy if someone would post the part numbers of these
: larger/faster cache chips.
Look into your AXPpci33 OEM design guide ;)
You need 128k x 8 chips with either 20ns or 15ns in 32-pin DIP package.
Nearly any type should work. The AXPpci33 is pretty standard...
The board only has the wider sockets for those but the wider variant of
those chips is out of production for a long time. But even the pins of the
smaller package can be bent a little to fit into the wider sockets. Someone
once mentioned that the indeed only 256k chips works in the smaller 'inner'
sockets...

: Anybody?
