In article <36E0A206.62E7C3CF@feist.com>, Ron Flory wrote:
>hi-
>
> I'm trying to build a x86-hosted cross-compiler for my Multia, but I
>have have yet to stuble upon an 'alpha' target spec that gcc-2.7.2.3
>will accept.  the binutils have already built, without a hitch.
>
>  --target=alpha-linux 
>
> is not recognized- anybody know what I should use ?

1) gcc-2.7.2.3 will not target linux-alpha out of the box.  The
version distributed with RedHat (5.0?) had some major patches applied
to it.  If you want to build gcc for linux-alpha, you'll need
gcc-2.8.1 or egcs.

2) To the best of my knowledge, it is impossible to build a
cross-compiler from a 32-bit host to a 64-bit target.  Something to do
with gcc assuming that a target word will fit into a host word.

HTH,
-andy



