 "Jurrie Lulofs" <jurrie@ipass.net> writes:
> I'd appreciate hearing about experiences from others
> wrt cache on low-end Alpha boxes.

We have a 300MHz 21064A (Cabriolet) that was pretty slow at compiling
the kernel and other tasks with 0K L2.  Then we installed 512K of 15ns
cache (the slowest for this machine), and performance became pretty
decent (comparable to the other Cabriolets we have, with 2M cache).

So, if you can find cache (any size) for your box, install it.

