It is my *opinion* (I have no facts to back it up) that with "slow"
RAM cache is good to have... I would really suggest you
consider getting the 256K cache for your board - it is *really*
cheap (the chips needed were very common on old 486
motherboards - that's where I got mine!). I would imagine it
would make your system 10-15% faster, but that is a guess.

I have been told by others that  the 1 Meg cache for these
boards is not worth it, since the price is *about* $15/chip
IF you can find them...

Good luck - check the manual for your system, take note of
the cache chips that work (Winbond I think) and start going
through parts bins at computer fairs - for a few bucks your
system should be a bit faster...

HTH,

