A couple of items.... 

1) use 2.2.1 as 2.2.2 will not compile on alpha, only on i386.
   although there is a patch set to make it compile on the alpha
   I had very poor luck with it.

2) On the alpha you do:

   make dep
   make clean
   make boot (there is no make zimage on the alpha port)
   make modules (if necessary)
   cp arch/alpha/boot/vmlinux.gz /tvmlinux.gz
   make modules_install (if using modules)

   reboot and use the /tvmlinux.gz image to test it. If it
   is working ok for you then rename it to /vmlinux.gz, saving
   a copy of the previous working kernel as ovmlinux.gz or something.

: I use Redhat 5.2 distribution. Thanks in advance.


