On Mon, 1 Mar 1999, Joseph Sarkes wrote:

> Seems there may be a paging bug in there somewhere. Still, I don't see
> any way to trace back without a core dump, which does not occur. The
> machine just suddenly goes south. Stops in mid-step and tries to get back

Hi Joseph,

Which 2.2.2 are you running?  My understanding is that the stock one is
broken (to even be compiled) on all arch's other than i386.  I'd first
suggest trying 2.2.1 to see if the problem is present there.  In any case,
you can try to debug the problem further by building your kernel with
debugging symbols (add a "-g" to the CFLAGS line in the top-level
Makefile).  Wait for the Oops/machine check again and write down the PC
address.  Then you can run gdb on the kernel:
"(cd /usr/src/linux; gdb vmlinux -c /proc/kcore)" and try to list out the
offending piece of code with "l *0xbad-address".

Good luck,
-bp
