steven fierens (steven.fierens@vub.ac.be) wrote:
: Hi!

: I recently bought an NoName AXPpci 33 board with a 166MHz Alpha on it.
: Should I really buy ECC memory chips (which I can't seem to find), or is
: it OK to just use parity SIMMS ?  Would it be harmfull to my brand-new
: (albeit inexpensive) motherboard to try it with the wrong SIMMS ?

The multia, which I am pretty sure is the same basic hardware as what
you have, uses 72 pin parity simms. Since it uses a pair at a time,
it gets 64 bits data and 8 bits of parity (used for some type of
hamming parity code for error correction). I think i read somewhere
that you need 70nSec parity ram, and that is what I think I have.
If you don't have parity, i understand the machine locks up without
doing much more than blink a led someplace.

